 are very private on your  instagram like you don't show much of  your personal life  it's is that intentional like are you  dating in quarantine right now  i have an interesting relationship with  instagram sort of the same kind of  relationship that people do with their  bank accounts where they don't really  want to log in and see  listen  i'm not i'm not intentionally not  sharing  i just frankly don't think that what i'm  doing  is like so spectacular that it needs to  be  put out there yeah and the love wellness  instagram account  does most of my work for me at this  point okay  that's really you know the message and  the story that i want to get behind  um and so you can see a lot of myself  there through the messaging and through  what we're trying to do as a brand  will you ever show the personal aspect  of yourself on your own  instagram like if there's a special  person  yeah i'm sure at some point and like i  do  here and there you know what i mean but  it's just not my focus  to be honest with you what does the next  five years look like for you  both professionally and personally for  me i'm really excited to continue  to grow love wellness as a brand  to continue to create new products and i  would love to  have a home in california and spend more  time with my family  and and that's it i think it's been a  really interesting year  so far and so there's so many question  marks on the future  and i've just gotten way more  comfortable with taking it day by day


